        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-11T11:57:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I like your theory about Fright Train. Have you checked the timing of the relevant comic issues? But on this point:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"ClericalError\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/clericalerror/48/2396_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ClericalError:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The effects of Time Cataclysm still prevelant and Tachyon's research lab spewing all kinds of Multiverse research everywhere fused the two timeline versions of her. With Freedom Tower and the timing of the attack, Miss Information was born from  <em>Vengeance</em> .&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think that it's clear from what we know now that the fusing of the two versions of Aminia Twain was not some sort of accident, but was OblivAeon trying to undermine the heroes of the main-timeline Earth, who were interfering with his master plan.</p>",
